                        "span": {
                          "lg": 2
                        },
                        "name": "test case description",
                        "content": {
                          "text": [
                            {
                              "locale": "en",
                              "text": "<p>In this test case the form validation should highlight modeling issues that occur when document and form model contradict each other.</p>\n<p>That is why the master field in the following form is connected to the other fields using the different kinds of dependencies:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>dependent field</li>\n<li>dependent enumeration</li>\n<li>dependent group</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Thus, whenever the master field changes the connected fields are changed as well.</p>\n<p>Any such change to the master field is validated and this validation should take all changed fields and their interconnection via validation rules into account.</p>\n<p>How to test</p>\n<ul>\n<li>When selecting 'A' everything should be fine.</li>\n<li>When selecting 'B' or 'C' a number of validation errors should immediately be presented since the validation rules in the document model are in conflict with the dependencies in the form model.\n<ul>\n<li>The selection of B should make slave, numField, stringField and Error Field invalid. The errors for numField and stringField will only be shown immediately if their values were not empty before selecting B.</li>\n<li>The selection of C should make only slave and numField invalid.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>"
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "Row",
                    "id": "row-91a6d",
